    "text": "By Hannah Barthels ,\n1 days ago The image of a sleek, perfectly fitted Holstein parading around the colored shavings at World Dairy Expo often conjures thoughts of purebred passion and genetic art: something that doesn’t always seem to fit with the daily grind of commercial milk production. Yet farms like GenoSource and Woldt Farms are among a growing number of forward-thinking operations proving this dichotomy false. Read full article",
